{
  "rules": [
    "Late-horizon upside bias: from ~day 18–30 the model persistently underestimates rising markets; apply an increasing positive adjustment with horizon (≈ +1 to +2 €/t by day 20, rising to ≈ +3 to +6 €/t by day 30 when the realized path trends up).",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: the model reacts too slowly to regime shifts from downtrend to uptrend (misses the convexity of the rebound). If the last 5–10 days show a clear reversal (higher highs/higher lows), tilt the whole forecast path upward and steepen the slope.",
    "Underestimation after breakouts: when spot breaks above the recent 10–15d range, the model mean-reverts too aggressively and caps the move. In breakout conditions, reduce mean-reversion strength and allow higher terminal levels (raise upper tail).",
    "Horizon-dependent error structure: near-term (days 1–7) errors are small and roughly unbiased; keep minimal correction there, concentrate corrections on mid/long horizon (days 10–30).",
    "Asymmetry in rising vs falling regimes: the model performs worse in rallies than in declines (systematic negative bias during rallies). Use a regime switch: if recent momentum is positive, add a bullish bias; if momentum is negative/flat, apply little or no bias correction."
  ]
}
